! PROGRESSIVE INDEXING WITH X0 IS OPERATION CODE INVALID, and this
! pins it against the printed rule rather than against the model.
!
! >>> THE REFUSAL WAS IN THE MODEL, UNCITED, IN BOTH VFL ARMS. <<<
! Reference Manual printed p.21 (PDF 24), read at the ink:
!
!   "In progressive indexing, the value field, bits 0-24 of the index
!   specified by I, is used as the effective address.  IF PROGRESSIVE
!   INDEXING WITH INDEX REGISTER X0 IS SPECIFIED, INDICATOR OP
!   (OPERATION CODE INVALID) IS SET."
!
! Index field 0 means "no indexing" for ordinary addressing -- see
! effAddr24's `if (idx == 0) return raw` -- so progressive indexing has
! no register to advance and the machine refuses it.
!
! WHY IT NEEDED A DECK: it is one of the six causes of
! StretchIBox's prepareExec.completesWithoutFetch, and a census of
! which causes the corpus reaches (docs/ebox_roadmap.md) found this one
! and the decimal refusal firing ZERO times in 5621 checks.  They were
! reasoned from the arms rather than measured.
!
! THE POSITIVE CONTROL IS THE POINT.  A deck that only asserts "OP came
! on" passes if nothing works at all, so the legal non-progressive store
! runs first and its target is checked for the value it must have.  X0
! is loaded with TB's address, so the refused store names a real word:
! if the refusal ever stops happening, TB changes and the check says so.
        SLC, (8)300.0
START   LV, $X0, TBADDR
        L(BU,6,6), DATA2
        ST(BU,6,6), TA+.60           ! legal, non-progressive
        BOP, $                       ! hang if OP came on: that one is legal
        ST(V+I)(BU,6,6), .6($X0)     ! PROGRESSIVE WITH X0 -- p.21 says OP
        BZOP, $                      ! hang if OP did NOT come on
        B, PASS
PASS    BEW, $
        CNOP
        SLC, (8)400.0
DATA2   DD(BU,6), (8)46
        SLC, (8)401.0
TBADDR  VF, TB+.60
        SLC, (8)410.0
TA      DD(BU,64), (8)1777777777777777777777
        DD(BU,64), (8)1777777777777777777777
        SLC, (8)420.0
TB      DD(BU,64), (8)1777777777777777777777
        DD(BU,64), (8)1777777777777777777777
        END, START
